    "statement": "At n_independent = 4, M-43's paired-difference criterion fires on 75% of draws on average and on only 24% at h=8. That estimate is an UPPER BOUND on the power the rule actually had: it subsamples a pool that is in-sample for these arms, where the effect is +0.425 to +0.790, against +0.204 to +0.545 on the held-out pair the rule is stated over. So the rule was under-powered at n=4 -- decisively at h=8 -- and we do not claim it could not have passed, only that it was committed without anyone checking what it could detect."
